{#
  The primary navigation, previously duplicated across 8 files and drifted in
  four different ways. The variations were real, not accidental, so they are
  parameters rather than something to flatten:

    pageKey         which link gets .is-active; "home" also makes the logo and
                    Home link scroll to #top instead of reloading the page
    navCtaHref      the desktop button — free-audit retargets it to #request
    navCtaLabel     …and its label
    navCtaCurrent   adds aria-current="page" when the button targets this page
    mobileCta1/2    the two mobile buttons — contact swaps the second for a
                    tel: link, free-audit reorders and relabels both

  Labels stay literal English here. Phase 3 moves them into the locale bundles.
#}
{#
  Front matter is plain YAML and cannot evaluate {{ urls.* }}, so a page that
  needs a button pointed at a different page names the route instead — e.g.
  mobileCta2Route: "contact" — and the lookup happens here. An explicit
  *Href still wins, for the off-site and anchor targets.
#}
{#
  Href resolution order, highest first:
    *Href     an explicit literal — anchors like "#request"
    *Contact  a key in site.contact — "phoneHref" for the tel: link
    *Route    a key in urls — "contact"
    otherwise the partial's own default

  Labels run through a {phone} placeholder so the number lives in one place
  even when it appears inside a sentence: "Call {phone}".
#}
{#
  The links themselves come from `menu[locale.code]` (src/_data/menu.js), which
  reads the sections out of the client's seed content tree. Adding a directory
  under branding/<client>/content/<locale>/ adds a menu item here and in
  the footer; nothing in this file is edited to rebrand the template.

  An item carries either a `labelKey` — a page whose translated label already
  lives in the locale bundle — or a `label` read from the section's own
  index.md. `key` doubles as the pageKey a page declares in its front matter,
  so the active link is still marked without a URL comparison on routed pages.
#}
{% set homeHref = "#top" if pageKey == "home" else urls.home %}
{% set navCtaHref = navCtaHref | default(site.contact[navCtaContact] if navCtaContact else (urls[navCtaRoute] if navCtaRoute else urls.freeAudit)) %}
{% set navCtaLabel = navCtaLabel | default(t.common.nav.ctaFreeAudit) %}
{% set mobileCta1Href = mobileCta1Href | default(site.contact[mobileCta1Contact] if mobileCta1Contact else (urls[mobileCta1Route] if mobileCta1Route else urls.contact)) %}
{% set mobileCta1Label = mobileCta1Label | default(t.common.nav.mobileBookCall) %}
{% set mobileCta2Href = mobileCta2Href | default(site.contact[mobileCta2Contact] if mobileCta2Contact else (urls[mobileCta2Route] if mobileCta2Route else urls.freeAudit)) %}
{% set mobileCta2Label = mobileCta2Label | default(t.common.nav.mobileFreeAudit) %}
  <!-- ============ NAVIGATION ============ -->
  <header class="nav" id="nav">
    <div class="container nav__inner">
      <a href="{{ homeHref }}" class="nav__logo" aria-label="{{ t.common.nav.logoAria | safe }}">
        <img src="{{ site.logos.dark }}" alt="{{ t.common.nav.logoAlt | safe }}" />
      </a>
      <nav class="nav__links" aria-label="{{ t.common.nav.primaryAria | safe }}">
{% for item in menu[locale.code] %}{% set label = t.common.nav[item.labelKey] if item.labelKey else item.label %}{% set href = homeHref if item.key == "home" else item.url %}{% set isActive = (pageKey and (item.key == pageKey or item.routeKey == pageKey)) or (item.url != urls.home and page.url.startsWith(item.url)) %}        <a href="{{ href }}"{% if isActive %} class="is-active"{% endif %}>{{ label | safe }}</a>
{% endfor %}      </nav>
      <div class="nav__actions">
{#
  The call-to-action button that sat here pointed at whichever landing page the
  template shipped — free-audit by default. Those pages are a design decision a
  client makes, not something the nav can assume, so the button comes back when
  there is a page for it to point at.
#}
{% set variant = "desktop" %}{% include "partials/lang-switcher.njk" %}
      </div>
      <button class="nav__toggle" id="navToggle" aria-label="{{ t.common.nav.toggleAria | safe }}" aria-expanded="false">
        <span></span><span></span><span></span>
      </button>
    </div>
    <!-- Mobile menu -->
    <div class="nav__mobile" id="navMobile">
{% for item in menu[locale.code] %}{% set label = t.common.nav[item.labelKey] if item.labelKey else item.label %}{% set href = homeHref if item.key == "home" else item.url %}      <a href="{{ href }}">{{ label | safe }}</a>
{% endfor %}{% set variant = "mobile" %}{% include "partials/lang-switcher.njk" %}
    </div>
  </header>
